    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) and **Seiya Suzuki** (73.90) leading our offensive production. **Vinnie Pasquantino** is our top play, benefiting from a massive +16% park factor and a favorable matchup against Baz, whose 4.62 xERA provides the high-ceiling environment needed to maximize points. **Seiya Suzuki** also thrives in his placement against Abbott, where a strong platoon advantage and a premium #2 spot in the lineup amplify his base projection. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** (69.47) and **Corbin Carroll** (67.54) represent our core stolen base threats; **Mickey Moniak** is particularly intriguing against McDonald, as his +14% platoon edge and the opponent's slow delivery to the plate create an ideal scenario to exploit our scarcity in SB. **James Wood** rounds out the elite tier with a 66.26 score, buoyed by an elite 0.434 xwOBA that remains a force regardless of the opponent.\n\nThe toughest decision on today\u2019s bench involved **Austin Riley** (46.66). Despite his pedigree, **Austin Riley** narrowly missed the start because his matchup against May is suppressed by adverse wind conditions and a bottom-third order placement, dropping him behind the more efficient profile of **Kyle Karros**. We are closely monitoring the risk profile for **Brice Turang** (45.98) and **Jose Caballero** (45.56); both find themselves in high-stress matchups against top-tier arms in Skenes and Cavalli, respectively. **Brice Turang** specifically faces a -19% SP skill penalty, making him a volatile play despite his high-upside speed profile. We are proceeding with this lineup to maximize daily efficiency, while keeping **Josh Naylor**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Cole Young** on standby to preserve our remaining game caps should weather or late lineup shifts necessitate a pivot.",
